You would like to dress him with "some" armor.  Just not "this" armor.
Carefully read the description of a marilith and you will be able to
figure out what pieces of armor he will be able to wear and what types
he will not.  The shape of a monster will determine what types or
armor it can wear.

> He's wielding a +0 long sword, but she also found a +1 battle axe which 
> she would like to "arm" him with.
> By default, shoulden't such a pet keep particular armour/weapons unless 
> better of the same is found ?

Pets use a very good list of what weapons to select.  The exact list
is in the weapons spoiler file.  A battle axe is well above a long sword.
The list is generated against the expected damage a weapon does, so it
is a very usefull list for characters before they get artifact weapons.

One problem with the list that isn't obvious on the surface: If you
don't know which weapons are one-handed and which weapons are two-handed,
you may not understand why a pet won't switch.  A pet already wearing a
shield might never give up that shield to switch to a two-handed weapon
and vice versa.

Also, a marilith wielding a good artifact weapon like Fire Brand does
amazing damage to the monsters it attacks.

